## ⚙️ Link Actions — Decide What Happens to URLs

🔗 Not every link you send needs to become a download.

🧩 Transloader's **Link Actions** let you define what should happen to links based on their URL scheme or host.

### 🛠️ Route Links Automatically

🌐 A particular website can be configured to open through another application instead of being downloaded by Transloader.

🔗 Specific URL schemes can also trigger supported applications, Automator workflows, or Shortcuts.

| 🔗 Link Condition  | ⚙️ Possible Action                          |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |
| 🌐 Specific Host   | 🖥️ Open with a selected application        |
| 🔗 URL Scheme      | 🧩 Trigger a configured workflow            |
| 📄 Web Document    | 🌐 Handle through the preferred application |
| 🤖 Automation Link | ⚡ Run a Shortcut or Automator workflow      |
| 📥 Download Link   | 🚀 Send to Transloader                      |

### 🎯 Example Workflow

📄 Imagine you regularly encounter links to online documents that you don't want Transloader to download.

🧩 Create a Link Action for that website or URL pattern.

🌐 Transloader can then route matching links to the application or workflow you selected.

